            "review_text": "Trực hồ\nVietnam2 contributions\n0\nI used to hate live food but was conquered here.\nApr 2026 • Friends\nI was extremely \"allergic\" to live fish dishes, listening to Sashimi that I often went away for fear of the hard-eating flavor. However, after a night of visit by a colleague, I realized that I had long since missed a true aspect of the sea. It turns out that the food is not as scary as you think, it is important that you enjoy the \"fine\" food and the standard freshness process.\nSurfing through a few reviews that say here peak price or thin slice of fish, I found that angle a little sorry for a true culinary experience. For people who have gone to work and are getting harder at choosing quality meals like us, what we need is qualification, not quantity. Here, each piece of salmon or tuna belly gets fattened, watered and melted right on top of the tongue. It is the price of original freshness, no need to use filled rice or excessive fever to lick the original taste. Enjoying here is enjoying the class of a real restaurant, where each dish is a work of art rather than a rushing meal to fill the stomach.\nThe most impressive thing is the skill of the staff. You observe very good guests, support very fast and professional, creating a sense of being cared for without bothering. If you’re looking for a quiet space to talk to your partner, or simply want to “hide” from the bullshit, noise after a long, stressful day at work, then Yen is an incredible choice.\nThis place is not for drinks, but for those who value privacy and personalized service. Although the price is higher than the general level, it is true that it is \"expensive to cut out.\" To be absolutely relaxed and reach the height of taste in a luxurious space like this, I believe it is absolutely deserved!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten April 1, 2026",
